From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: resume pending AC restoration after daemon restart

Keep pending, completed and cancelled policy state in /run for this kernel
boot. Snapshot the pre-AC state, selected policy and boot-relative deadline
so a daemon restart resumes only an unconsumed restore request. Completed
policies, manual power actions and BIOS-managed power remain consumed.
Retain the programming interlock when a pending restore is retried.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD AC restore lifecycle]

